        "event": "Special Weather Statement",
        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 29 at 5:07AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "Daytime high temperatures will reach 70 to 75 degrees throughout\nthis week, and will be hottest today and tomorrow. Temperatures\nthis warm, and for this long, happen about once per year.\n\nThe long duration of warmer days may impact subsistence\nactivities like berry picking, fishing, and hunting. This could\nalso affect people who are extremely sensitive to heat (like\nelders or infants), especially if they are unable to cool down or\nstay hydrated.\n\nActions: Keep homes cool by closing curtains duri",
