        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 28 at 3:31PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "Water levels are expected to rise to 1 to 2 feet above the normal\nhigh tide line around Baldwin Peninsula and northern coastlines\nof the Kotzebue Sound, peaking in the early morning and\ndiminishing rapidly Wednesday afternoon as the cold front moves\nthrough. Gusty westerly winds 20 to 30 mph will occur.",
